-//     2^(w-2) unbalanced increments would otherwise be reachable and wrap
-//     the count. (With w = 64 that is > 4 * 10^18 increments: unreachable,
-//     so the increment stays guard-free on 64-bit targets.)
+//     false. In the immortal encoding `rc.inc`'s store is steered away from
+//     a recognized dummy as well. Under TBI the increment stays guard-free
+//     and does land on the dummy: its count word is 32 bits, so 2^32
+//     references wrap it through 0 and 1. The decrement expansion therefore
